# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/

# Secrets and environment.
#
# The negation on the last line is load-bearing: `.env.*` matches `.env.example`,
# so without it the committed template would be silently ignored and every fresh
# clone would have no idea which keys the project wants. Order matters in a
# gitignore - the exception has to come after the rule it overrides.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Local editor / agent settings. Machine-specific, not part of the experiment.
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived outputs, under runs/.
#
# These are ignored by default and force-added when they are real. The reason is
# not disk space: a mock run writes files full of plausible percentages that
# measure nothing, and a fabricated number that reaches the repository is the
# single most likely way one gets quoted as a measurement.
#
# `git add -f runs/results.wide.jsonl` is therefore the deliberate act that
# publishes a ladder's run, and `run_eval.guard_clobber` blocks a mock run from
# overwriting a real one on the way there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/results.*.jsonl
runs/frontier.*.jsonl
runs/sweep_degraded.*.jsonl
runs/results.*.bak
runs/run_all_ladders.log

# Figures were ignored while the inputs were simulated - a chart is far more
# likely than a table to be screenshotted without its caption - on the condition,
# written here, that they be committed once there was a real run behind them.
# There is: all three ladders were measured on 10 August 2026.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw model-response cache.
#
# cache/raw_calls.<ladder>.jsonl holds REAL responses and is deliberately NOT
# ignored. It is the whole point: committing it is what lets someone with no API
# key reproduce every number here for $0.00 via ROUTER_MODE=replay.
#
# cache/routellm_scores.jsonl is likewise committed, which is what lets the
# routellm policy run without torch, a checkpoint download, or a GPU.
#
# The .mock.jsonl siblings ARE ignored: they are fabricated, they regenerate for
# free in seconds, and a separate file per mode means a simulated response can
# never be one careless `git add` away from being published as a measurement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache/*.mock.jsonl
cache/*.tmp
cache/*.lock
cache/*.bak

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Personal prep notes, never published.
BRIEFING.local.md
